The bug is that for odd n, we are calculating ((n + 1) / 2) * ((n + 1) / 2), but it should be (n / 2) * (n / 2). This is because when n is odd, the middle element will be the target value and all other elements need to be adjusted to reach that value. The correct formula for both cases is simply (n/2)^2.

```java
class Solution {
    public int minOperations(int n) {
        int result = 0;

        if (n % 2 == 0) {
            result = (n / 2) * (n / 2);
        } else {
            result = (n / 2) * (n / 2);
        }

        return result;
    }
}
